{"id": "unknown-2026-05-22-007", "date": "2026-05-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.33, "keywords": ["improve", "decline", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "US Upland cotton sales rebound after steep decline: USDA", "content": "US Upland cotton export sales rebounded to 131,800 RB in the week ending May 14, 2026, after the previous week’s sharp fall.\nPakistan led buying, followed by Vietnam and Turkiye, while new-crop sales surged to 216,000 RB.\nShipments stayed below the recent average.\nPima sales improved slightly but remained weak, with India the top buyer and destination.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/us-upland-cotton-sales-rebound-after-steep-decline-usda-310491-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-22-008", "date": "2026-05-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "EuroCham Cambodia’s White Book 2027 calls for regulatory reforms", "content": "EuroCham in Cambodia has launched the White Book 2027, urging the country to accelerate reforms and modernise its economy as it prepares for graduation from the LDC status in 2029. \nIgor Driesmans, Ambassador of the Delegation of the European Union to Cambodia, described the White Book as a timely, practical and solution-oriented road map aligned with Cambodia’s Pentagonal Strategy reform agenda. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/eurocham-cambodia-s-white-book-2027-calls-for-regulatory-reforms-310488-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-22-009", "date": "2026-05-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.75, "keywords": ["plunge", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "ICE cotton drops sharply as overbought market triggers sell-off", "content": "ICE cotton futures plunged sharply as overbought conditions triggered aggressive liquidation across contracts.\nThe July 2026 contract fell 4.4 per cent to settle at 77.98 cents per pound, slipping below the key 80-cent mark for the first time since April 29.\nFavourable US weather, easing crop risks, a stronger dollar and weak broader markets weighed heavily on sentiment.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-drops-sharply-as-overbought-market-triggers-sell-off-310489-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-22-010", "date": "2026-05-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s Vishal Fabrics FY26 PAT rises 23%, income 5%", "content": "Indian denim fabric manufacturer Vishal Fabrics has reported a 23 per cent YoY rise in FY26 PAT to ₹35.64 crore (~$3.70 million), while total income grew 5 per cent to ₹1,603.25 crore (~$166.42 million). \nQ4 FY26 PAT increased 22 per cent YoY. \nThe company attributed its performance to operational efficiencies, steady demand, value-added products, and resilient supply chains. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/india-s-vishal-fabrics-fy26-pat-rises-23-income-5--310480-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-22-011", "date": "2026-05-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "India’s Page Industries' FY26 PAT grows 4.8% to $76.4 mn", "content": "Page Industries has reported steady FY26 growth, with revenue rising 6.3 per cent YoY to ₹52.47 billion (~$524.7 million).\nMeanwhile, EBITDA went up 8.5 per cent to ₹11.53 billion (~$115.3 million), and PAT increased 4.8 per cent. \nIn Q4 FY26, sales volume grew 10.8 per cent, revenue rose 14.1 per cent, EBITDA increased 10.7 per cent, and PAT grew 9 per cent, supported by healthy demand. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/india-s-page-industries-fy26-pat-grows-4-8-to-76-4-mn-310474-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
